{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+16{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+16{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +16] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\\text{4i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{\\text{4i}}}={e}^{\\text{4i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x), \\\\ {x}^{-\\text{4i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-\\text{4i}}}={e}^{-\\text{4i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{\\text{4i}}+B{x}^{-\\text{4i}} \\\\ y(x) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\ y(x) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{c}_{2}}{4{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x)"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"]] "category"