tituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +7] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ {t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+7))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+7))"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{7}+{c}_{2}{t}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93816" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+3t{y}^{′}+18y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+3t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+18{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 3\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+3\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+18{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+3\\lambda +18] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+3\\lambda +18 & =0 \\\\ 3{\\lambda }^{2}+18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ {t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+6))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+6))"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+9y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+9{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+9{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +9] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 3\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{3\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t), \\\\ {t}^{-3\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-3\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{3\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-3\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_