ld" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-3t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-3\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda +7] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda +7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =-3 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={t}^{2}{e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)), \\\\ {t}^{2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={t}^{2}{e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B{t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B){t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B){t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as \n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)=t({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3))"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] ["math" "y(t