re, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+7\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+13 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$\n\nNote that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{-3+2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{-3}{e}^{\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)), \\\\ {t}^{-3-2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{-3}{e}^{-\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{-3+2\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B{t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B){t}^{-3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B){t}^{-3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-64849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3t)"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{-2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+2y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{t}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\sqrt{2}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-2))"] ["math" "y(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-5,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=-5$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & ={c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-93894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+32y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+2x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+32{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+2\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+32{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+2\\lambda +32] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+2\\lambda +32 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+32 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$  \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{x}^{4\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-4\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{4\\text{i}}}={e}^{4\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\ {x}^{-4\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-4\\text{i}}}={e}^{-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{4\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have set ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$  \n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=0.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4{x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =4{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c82de05a6ee9ebc9da262c7e07097557d386092961ee49ef5e1de5f6262d4318"} {"question" "q-64850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} {"question" "q-64850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"] ["math" "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070256/state.json" "file_sha256" "c6f6a17d3fd88ef5b4ee08d09fd3cfe2b030d695e7b9f7bae4f8899a10202340"} 